# No AI co-authors in commits

Never add AI tools or agents as commit co-authors.

## Forbidden

Do **not** include any of these in commit messages (subject or body):

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <…>`
- `Co-authored-by: cursoragent@…`
- `Co-authored-by:` for Claude, Copilot, ChatGPT, Gemini, Devin, Codex, or any other AI/agent identity
- Trailers like `Signed-off-by:` that name an AI agent
- Phrases such as “Generated by Cursor” / “Co-authored with AI” in the commit message

## Required

- Commit messages credit **human** authors only (the repo’s configured `user.name` / `user.email`).
- When creating or amending commits, strip any AI co-author trailer if the tooling inserts one.
- Prefer a plain conventional commit body with no attribution trailers unless the user explicitly asks for a **human** co-author.
- `aiskillgrid install` also installs a git `commit-msg` hook (`packs/git-hooks/commit-msg`) that strips these trailers automatically.

## Examples

```text
# ❌ BAD
feat(tools): managed npm install

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
feat(tools): managed npm install
```
